bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_call_to_function_named_pass_segfaults_2026-11-28, 0, "A call to a user function named pass segfaults under the seed JIT (rc 139) and is rejected by the interpreter with error: semantic: value is not callable. Minimal: fn pass(o: i64) -> i64: o + 1 / fn main(): print(pass(4)). Strict JIT (SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=jit SIMPLE_JIT_STRICT=1) dumps core on the base seed dc41771399af764f, on dd4adb4888424f68 and on the same binary with SIMPLE_NO_F64_OPTION_INLINE=1, so it is not caused by the f64? inline layout. Found in review as pass(Some(4.0)) crashing in a fixture where the parameter is stored into a local and read inside a transient scope (scratchpad rv_f64/t6.spl, case s4); renaming the function to thru makes that exact fixture print s4 8.0 on JIT and interpreter, so the transient-scope pattern is not the cause. pass is a statement keyword: the declaration is accepted, but the call site does not resolve to the function. Expected: either a compile error at fn pass (reserved word) or a working call; never a JIT segfault. Fix direction: reject pass as a function name in the parser / HIR lowering with a diagnostic, or resolve the callee to the declared function; and make the JIT refuse a non-callable callee instead of emitting an indirect call through it."

